From df98c367ae21948cdaa97cf569d9d506519c6e11 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:20:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): never hand a placement placeholder or foreign
 chat on as a child card's origin [daveey]

Defect kanban-69709bcf16. A hub worker on a card the MacBook placed (session_id
kanban-placement-macbook, the kanban.placement creator placeholder) called kanban_create;
the child routed to the MacBook and _handle_create took the parent card's session_id
unchecked as its origin. The MacBook asked hub to bind the card to that 'chat', hub refused
(origin_session_missing) and the rejection reached David's Inbox.

- the parent card's session_id now goes through _persisted_session_id like every other source
- _persisted_session_id also rejects placement placeholders: hub's state.db gained a
  kanban-placement-macbook row from a stray completion notice, so presence alone is not proof

Test: tests/tools/test_kanban_placeholder_origin.py (3 red before: origin_session was the
placeholder / a missing chat; a real chat still passes through).
